            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0313" n="218" xml:id="pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7996: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-24T08:00:00+08:00">June 24, 1936—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 24—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>198. 1. Foreign Office has issued a denial of Japanese press reports that Suma
                    gave Chinese Minister of Foreign Affairs on June 19th a “stern warning” against
                    the “continuation of malicious propaganda” against Japan.</p>
                <p>2. To Department, by mail to Peiping and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
